From cccde30bc7fdec3f6819981d1b7fcb33e1bbff7b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 12:26:51 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(post): grblHAL, Carvera and TinyG write no motion after
 the no-plane refusal

xyFirst returns false when it refuses the first X/Y traverse for want of a
stated ClearancePlane or RetractPlane, and onRapid, onLinear, onCircular
(and grblHAL's onCycle) then write nothing for the move - nor for any later
one while X/Y stay unknown. Before, the refused rapid was still written as
a combined G0 X.. Y.. Z.., which the post CLI put in the program text.
TinyG's onRapid had the same gap.

Fixes #1682

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
